      {
        "id": "ex-hh-minimal-representatives-for-s2-in-s3",
        "kind": "example",
        "title": "Minimal coset representatives of $S_2$ in $S_3$",
        "deps": [
          "def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length",
          "lem-hh-dihedral-root-recurrence-and-root-sign",
          "thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity",
          "def-coset",
          "def-finite-symmetric-group-and-permutation-notation",
          "ex-hh-type-a-reduced-words-and-inversions"
        ],
        "statement": "Let $W\\cong S_3$ be the type-A group of [[thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity]] (4) with $S=\\{s_1,s_2\\}$, and let $J=\\{s_1\\}$, so that $W_J=\\{1,s_1\\}\\cong S_2$. Then $W$ has three left cosets $W_Ja=\\{ua:u\\in W_J\\}$,\n\n$$\\{1,s_1\\},\\qquad \\{s_2,\\,s_1s_2\\},\\qquad \\{s_2s_1,\\,s_1s_2s_1\\},$$\n\nwith unique minimal elements $1$, $s_2$ and $s_2s_1$ of lengths $0$, $1$ and $2$. Each minimal element $d$ satisfies $\\ell(s_1d)>\\ell(d)$ (namely $\\ell(s_1)=1$, $\\ell(s_1s_2)=2$, $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3$), and length additivity holds: $\\ell(s_1\\cdot s_2)=1+1=2$ and $\\ell(s_1\\cdot s_2s_1)=1+2=3$. The corresponding right cosets $aW_J=\\{au:u\\in W_J\\}$ have the minimal representatives $1$, $s_2$, $s_1s_2$, and for these $\\ell(ds_1)=\\ell(d)+1$ holds.",
        "strategy": "1.1 **The parabolic subgroup.** $W_J=\\langle J\\rangle=\\langle s_1\\rangle=\\{1,s_1\\}$: the definition of $W_J$ as the subgroup generated by $J$ is [F5] and its identity with $\\langle s_1\\rangle$ is immediate for $J=\\{s_1\\}$ [F2]; the relator $s_1^2$ of the presentation gives $s_1^2=1$ [F5], so $\\langle s_1\\rangle\\subseteq\\{1,s_1\\}$, and $s_1\\ne1$ because $\\ell(s_1)=1$ [F6], so $\\langle s_1\\rangle$ has the two distinct elements $1,s_1$; it is a group of order $2$, hence isomorphic to $S_2$.\n\n1.2 **The right cosets.** The right cosets $aW_J$ are $\\{1,s_1\\}$, $s_2W_J=\\{s_2,s_2s_1\\}$ and $s_1s_2W_J=\\{s_1s_2,s_1s_2s_1\\}$, disjoint and exhausting $W$ by the six distinct elements listed in [F3]; their minimal elements are $1$ (length $0$), $s_2$ (length $1$, versus $\\ell(s_2s_1)=2$) and $s_1s_2$ (length $2$, versus $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3$), unique by the right-coset half of [F1]. For these three elements $d$ the right-handed additivity of [F1] gives $\\ell(ds_1)=\\ell(d)+\\ell(s_1)=\\ell(d)+1$, namely $\\ell(s_1)=1$, $\\ell(s_2s_1)=2=1+1$ and $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3=2+1$, as asserted; equivalently the right coset representatives satisfy the characterisation $\\ell(ds_1)>\\ell(d)$ of [F1].\n\n2.1 **The left cosets and their minimal elements.** For $W_J=\\{1,s_1\\}$ the sets $W_Ja=\\{ua:u\\in W_J\\}$ of [F4], with $a\\in W$, can be enumerated using the six-element list of [F3] they are $W_J\\cdot1=\\{1,s_1\\}$, $W_Js_2=\\{s_2,s_1s_2\\}$ and $W_Js_2s_1=\\{s_2s_1,s_1s_2s_1\\}$, which are disjoint and exhaust $W$. Reading the lengths off [F3], the minimum of $\\ell$ is $0$ on $\\{1,s_1\\}$ (attained at $1$), $1$ on $\\{s_2,s_1s_2\\}$ (attained at $s_2$) and $2$ on $\\{s_2s_1,s_1s_2s_1\\}$ (attained at $s_2s_1$); by [F1] each coset has a unique element of minimal length, so the minimal representatives are $1$, $s_2$ and $s_2s_1$ with lengths $0$, $1$ and $2$.\n\n3.1 **The descent characterisation and length additivity.** For the three minimal representatives $d=1$, $d=s_2$ and $d=s_2s_1$, the table of [F3] gives $\\ell(s_1\\cdot1)=\\ell(s_1)=1>0=\\ell(1)$, $\\ell(s_1s_2)=2>1=\\ell(s_2)$ and $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=3>2=\\ell(s_2s_1)$, so each of them satisfies the characterisation $\\ell(s_1d)>\\ell(d)$ of [F1]. The additivity identity of [F1] for $u=s_1\\in W_J$ reads $\\ell(s_1d)=\\ell(s_1)+\\ell(d)$ for the minimal $d$; at $d=s_2$ this is $\\ell(s_1s_2)=1+1=2$ and at $d=s_2s_1$ it is $\\ell(s_1s_2s_1)=1+2=3$, the two values asserted in the statement.\n\n4.1 **Collected.** The example enumerates the three left cosets and the three right cosets of $W_J=\\{1,s_1\\}$ in $W\\cong S_3$, identifies their unique minimal representatives with the lengths predicted by the parabolic theorem, verifies the descent characterisations on both sides and the length-additivity identities $\\ell(ud)=\\ell(u)+\\ell(d)$ and $\\ell(du)=\\ell(d)+\\ell(u)$ for $u=s_1$ (steps 2.1, 3.1, 1.2).",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "George Lusztig, Hecke Algebras with Unequal Parameters (revised book text, arXiv:math/0208154v2)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0208154",
              "locator": "Lemma 9.7, printed p. 40: unique minimal coset elements and l(yw)=l(y)+l(w)"
            },
            {
              "title": "Anders Bjorner and Francesco Brenti, Combinatorics of Coxeter Groups, Springer GTM 231 (2005) (complete author/class-hosted PDF)",
              "url": "https://sites.math.washington.edu/~billey/classes/reflection.groups/references/EntireBook.pdf",
              "locator": "Proposition 2.4.4 and Corollary 2.4.5, printed pp. 39-40: unique factorization W = W^J W_J with l(w)=l(w^J)+l(w_J)"
            }
          ]
